# cgw-install-batch.conf -- project list for cgw-batch-install.cmd
#
# One absolute project path per line. Each path must already be a
# CGW-managed project (i.e. it has a .cgw.conf from a prior run of
# cgw-install.cmd) -- projects without one are skipped with a warning,
# since this file drives an UPDATE, not a first-time install.
#
# - Lines starting with "#" are comments (the whole line is ignored).
# - Blank lines are ignored.
# - No globs/wildcards -- list each project directory explicitly.
#
# Copy this file to cgw-install-batch.conf (git-ignored) and edit the
# list below to match your machine.
#
# Usage:
#   cgw-batch-install.cmd                # update every project listed here
#   cgw-batch-install.cmd --dry-run       # preview only, no changes made
#   cgw-batch-install.cmd other.conf      # use a different list file
#
# Examples (edit/replace with your real project paths):
# C:\Users\me\Projects\my-web-app
# C:\Users\me\Projects\my-other-repo
# D:\Work\client-project
